.\" Manual page for docmost-cli-attachment(1)
.\" Source: SPECIFICATION.md section 4.6, src/docmost_cli/cli/attachment.py
.TH DOCMOST\-CLI\-ATTACHMENT 1 "2026\-03\-22" "docmost\-cli 0.4.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
docmost\-cli\-attachment \- attachment operations for Docmost wiki
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B docmost\-cli attachment search
.I query
.RB [ \-\-space
.IR slug ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.br
.B docmost\-cli attachment upload
.I page\-id
.BI \-\-file " path"
.RB [ \-\-replace
.IR attachment\-id ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-insert ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.br
.B docmost\-cli attachment info
.I attachment\-id
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.br
.B docmost\-cli attachment download
.I attachment\-id
.RB [ \-\-output
.IR path ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Commands for working with file attachments in a Docmost wiki.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.SS search
Search for attachments by name or content.
.PP
.I query
is the search string.
.TP
.BI \-\-space " slug"
Restrict search to attachments in a specific space.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Output as a JSON array instead of a Rich table.
.PP
Table columns: id, fileName, type.
.SS upload
Upload a file or image owned by
.I page\-id
and append it to the page content.
The stable attachment ID is written to stdout.
.TP
.BI \-\-file " path"
Local file to upload.
.TP
.BI \-\-replace " attachment\-id"
Replace an existing attachment's bytes while preserving its ID and URL.
The replacement must use the same file extension.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-insert
Create the attachment without appending a new content block.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Return the full attachment record including stable ID and authenticated URL.
.SS info
Show metadata and the stable authenticated URL for an attachment ID.
.SS download
Download an attachment by ID.
.TP
.BI \-\-output " path"
Destination file or directory.
.SH EXAMPLES
Search for attachments:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
$ docmost\-cli attachment search "architecture diagram"
.EE
.RE
.PP
Search within a space:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
$ docmost\-cli attachment search "logo" \-\-space design
.EE
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
See
.BR docmost\-cli (1).
